sgl-project/sglang:python/sglang/srt/kv_canary/api.py: speculative_num_steps = int(server_args.speculative_num_steps or 1)
sgl-project/sglang:docs/advanced_features/adaptive_speculative_decoding.md: Adaptive speculative decoding lets SGLang adjust `speculative_num_steps/speculative_num_draft_tokens` at runtime instead of keeping a single fixed value for the whole server lifetime.
sgl-project/sglang:docs/advanced_features/adaptive_speculative_decoding.md: `speculative_num_steps` controls how many draft-model autoregressive steps run in each speculative round. In practice, the best value depends on the current workload.
